the warnings had been ominous an attack  by the russian military would begin in  eastern ukraine before the sun would  rise a threat that russian president  vladimir putin followed through with  after weeks of developing a military  posture along ukraine's border  consisting of roughly two 200 000 troops  there was a global push late wednesday  to bring the kremlin back from the brink  the united nations security council  convening an emergency meeting tonight  russia has brought its people the  ukrainian people and the world  to the brink of a conflict that will  produce an untold amount of human  suffering bob ray canada's ambassador to  the u.n adding vladimir putin's war  crimes cannot go unanswered only minutes  after russian troops were told to lay  down their arms social media became a  window into the new reality showing the  impacts of what appeared to be missiles  being launched into ukraine the white  house quick to respond saying the world  will hold russia accountable noting it  will be responsible for the death and  destruction this attack will bring the  attack comes only days after an address  from vladimir putin decrying ukraine's  sovereignty arguing its government was  carrying out a genocide against ethnic  russians an unsubstantiated claim seen  as pretext for this assault  in a last attempt to stave off an  operation that threatened his country's  future ukraine's leader spoke to russian  citizens in their native tongue on the  devastation war will have on both  ukrainians and russians alike russia's  u.n envoy is not calling this a war  rather a special military operation one  the world attempted to stop using  sanctions that didn't act as a deterrent  and has left rules-based order under the  ultimate threat  reggie chikini global news washington
 

